Source of these files: the ONNX exports of the SAM 2.1 checkpoints packaged as sam2.1_hiera_tiny_20260221.zip and
sam2.1_hiera_large_20260221.zip (an image encoder and a prompt decoder each, as used by X-AnyLabeling).

What was changed: the image encoder was simplified for a fixed 1024 x 1024 input (onnxsim or onnxslim) and both
graphs were converted by tools/convert_onnx_model.py into NumPy files, with weights of 4096 values or more stored as
16-bit floats (the image features differ from the original's by about 0.1% on average; the outlines agree to 99.8%
intersection-over-union in our tests). They are run by the Studio's own NumPy code (studio/engine/local/onnxnp.py,
GPL-3.0); ONNX Runtime is not used.
